      "writtenOn": "2026-03-25T12:37:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the current kvm_pgtable.h, the following MACROs defined:\n#define KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_RW\t(KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_R | KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_W)\n#define KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_RWX\t(KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_RW | KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_X)\n\n#define PKVM_HOST_MEM_PROT\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_RWX\n#define PKVM_HOST_MMIO_PROT\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_RW\n\nSo, PKVM_HOST_MEM_PROT(R | W | X) includes PKVM_HOST_MMIO_PROT(R | W). But they don\u0027t include \"KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_PXN | KVM_PGTABLE_PROT_UXN\".\n\nenum kvm_pgtable_prot {\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_X\t\t\t\u003d BIT(0),\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_W\t\t\t\u003d BIT(1),\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_R\t\t\t\u003d BIT(2),\n\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_DEVICE\t\t\t\u003d BIT(3),\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_NORMAL_NC\t\t\u003d BIT(4),\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_PXN\t\t\t\u003d BIT(5),\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_UXN\t\t\t\u003d BIT(6),\n\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_SW0\t\t\t\u003d BIT(55),\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_SW1\t\t\t\u003d BIT(56),\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_SW2\t\t\t\u003d BIT(57),\n\tKVM_PGTABLE_PROT_SW3\t\t\t\u003d BIT(58),\n};",
